{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f0c2a54-3d1e-4b7a-9a52-1c8e7d4f2b60",
    "name": "Climate Alerts",
    "description": "Manual end-to-end walk through the climate alert API.\n\nSetup: run `docker compose up --build`, then `docker compose logs seed` and paste the tokens of user 1 and user 2 into `token_user_1` and `token_user_2` in the `Climate Alerts Local` environment. Give the worker a few seconds after startup: folder 6 expects the notifications from its first evaluation.\n\nRun the folders in order, because later requests use the `alert_id` captured by `Create alert`. The environment assumes a clean database, where user 1 owns field 1 and user 2 owns field 2.\n\nThe collection can be re-run: `7. Cleanup` soft-deletes its `hail` alert, which frees the slot. If a run stops before that folder, `Create alert` returns 409 until the alert is deleted.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
